---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import KbdDemo from "../../components/KbdDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Kbd"
  description="Keyboard keys and shortcut groups for hints, tooltips, and search footers."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Kbd</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows a keyboard key or a shortcut. Use it in text, tooltips, menu rows, and
    footer hints.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><KbdDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Kbd usage"
      code={`import { Kbd, KbdGroup } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/kbd";

<Kbd>Enter</Kbd>

<KbdGroup>
  <Kbd>⌘</Kbd>
  <Kbd>K</Kbd>
</KbdGroup>

<p>Press <Kbd>Esc</Kbd> to close.</p>

<span className="flex items-center gap-1.5">
  <Kbd variant="outline">↵</Kbd>
  Open
</span>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Kbd</code> renders a <code>kbd</code> element. It is 20px tall and at
      least 20px wide, so one symbol is square and a word gets padding.
      <code>variant</code> is <code>"default"</code>, a muted fill, or <code
        >"outline"</code
      >, a border on the surface color. Use outline on tinted strips, such as a
      search footer, and on highlighted rows. There is one size.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>KbdGroup</code> holds keys pressed together and spaces them 4px apart.
      It is also a <code>kbd</code>, which is how HTML marks a key combination.
      An <code>svg</code> inside a key is 12px unless you give it a size class.
    </p>
    <p>
      Keys ignore the pointer and cannot be selected, so a click on a row or
      button with a key inside still reaches that row or button.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Selected row</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Enter key on the highlighted row"
      code={`<CommandItem className="result">
  {title}
  <Kbd variant="outline" aria-hidden="true" className="result-enter">↵</Kbd>
</CommandItem>

/* CSS */
.result-enter { display: none; }
.result[data-selected] > .result-enter { display: inline-flex; }`}
    />
    <p>
      Hide the key until its row is highlighted. Mark it <code>aria-hidden</code
      > because the row already says it can be chosen.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Kbd is not focusable and has no role. Screen readers read its text. Some
      symbols, such as <code>⌘</code>, are read in odd ways, so put the action
      in words next to the key. For a key that shows only an icon, add visually
      hidden text inside it. Do not put <code>aria-label</code> on the key.
    </p>
    <p>
      Color changes follow the theme in 120ms and stop when reduced motion is
      requested. In forced colors mode every key gets a visible border.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The default key uses <code>--sprout-secondary</code> and <code
        >--sprout-muted</code
      >. The outline key uses <code>--sprout-surface</code> and <code
        >--sprout-line</code
      >. Radius follows <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
